Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 01:28:43 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] ZDC try X2: photon pair chosen by the Lambda hypothesis in
 the ZDC neutrals

Phase 4 (the Lambda bar fight), experiment X2_lambda_pairing, build label X2, on X1 (accepted).
FarForwardNeutralsReconstruction, ZDC Hcal only (lambdaPairingHcalZDC, default true): of the clusters
tagged as photons, keep the pair that best fits Lambda -> n pi0 -> n gamma gamma; the other tagged
clusters stay with the neutron. Each pair is fitted with the neutron made of every other cluster
(calibrated energy sum, leader position): depth from the gamma-gamma opening angle (pi0 constraint)
along the momentum-weighted slope, ranked by the fitted pi0 and Lambda masses plus the Lambda
decay-depth density (c*tau = 78.9 mm). Energies are never rescaled; the mass only ranks the pair.
Prediction (scripts/471 on X1's events, x1_zNL rule): S4a_tm per thrown Lambda -> n pi0 = 2.84 % mean
over 100-275 GeV and 5.45 % at 275 GeV (X1: 1.970 % / 4.309 %). Judged against X1_offline_chain.
Verdict: pending (recorded in the next commit on this branch).

